                "<b><code>pwd</code></b> (<i>print working directory</i>): Shows the full path of the directory you are currently in.",
                "<b><code>who</code> and <code>users</code> vs. <code>whoami</code></b>: Both <code>who</code> and <code>users</code> display all users currently logged in to the system, whereas <code>whoami</code> displays <b>who you are logged in as</b> (the effective username of the current shell user).",
                "<b><code>cd</code> Navigation Variants</b>: (1) <code>cd dir</code> changes the current directory to <code>dir</code>; (2) <code>cd ..</code> changes the current directory to <b>one level up</b> (parent directory); (3) <code>cd ~</code> (or bare <code>cd</code>) changes the current directory to the user's <b>home directory</b>; (4) <code>cd /</code> changes the current directory to the <b>root directory</b>."
