            {
              "h": "Worked Problem 3: Paging Effective Access Time (EAT) with TLB (Slide 8.37 & Final 2020 Q56)",
              "pts": [
                "<b>Formula (Slide 8.37)</b>: With TLB lookup time <code>ε</code>, main-memory access time <code>m</code>, and TLB hit ratio <code>α</code>:",
                "• On a <b>TLB Hit</b> (probability <code>α</code>): frame number is found in TLB + 1 memory access for data = <code>ε + m</code>.",
                "• On a <b>TLB Miss</b> (probability <code>1 − α</code>): TLB lookup + 1 memory access for page table + 1 memory access for data = <code>ε + 2m</code>.",
                "• <b><code>EAT = α(ε + m) + (1 − α)(ε + 2m) = (2 − α)m + ε</code></b>.",
                "<b>Slide 8.37 Example</b>: <code>ε = 20 ns</code>, <code>m = 100 ns</code>:",
                "• If <code>α = 80% (0.80)</code>: <code>EAT = 0.80 × (20 + 100) + 0.20 × (20 + 200) = 96 + 44 = <b>140 ns</b></code>.",
                "• If <code>α = 99% (0.99)</code>: <code>EAT = 0.99 × 120 + 0.01 × 220 = 118.8 + 2.2 = <b>121 ns</b></code>.",
                "<b>Final 2020 Q56 Example</b>: <code>ε = 0</code> (negligible), <code>m = 90 ms</code>, <code>α = 85% (0.85)</code>: <code>EAT = 0.85 × 90 + 0.15 × 180 = 76.5 + 27.0 = <b>103.5 ms</b></code>."
              ]
            }
