            "<b>Convoy Effect (Slide 6.12 — Final 2018 Q1.11, Final 2023 Q43, Final 2024 Q2)</b>: All other (short, I/O-bound) processes wait for one big CPU-bound process to get off the CPU, resulting in lower CPU and device utilization than if the shorter processes were allowed to go first."
