              "type": "mcq",
              "q": "55. Suppose process P0 executes `wait(S); wait(Q);` and process P1 executes `wait(Q); wait(S);` on binary semaphores S and Q initialized to 1. This leads to:",
              "o": [
                "starvation only",
                "deadlock",
                "high throughput",
                "automatic preemption"
              ],
              "a": 1,
              "why": "Slide 5.26: When P0 holds S and waits for Q while P1 holds Q and waits for S, a deadlock occurs."
