      "meta": "Cairo University · FCAI · CS341 Operating Systems · Prof. Khaled Wassif · 2020 (70 Marks)",
      "note": "Official 2020 Final Exam featuring 70 objective questions including TLB EAT math, Address Bit calculations, Round-Robin scheduling (`q=2`), and Page Replacement (`7,0,1,2...`).",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Key Objective & Calculation Questions from Final 2020",
          "marks": "Selected high-yield exam questions",
          "items": [
            {
              "type": "mcq",
              "q": "1 (Q36–37). Consider a logical address space of 128 pages of 2048 words each, mapped onto a physical memory of 64 frames. How many bits are there in the logical address and in the physical address?",
              "o": [
                "Logical = 18 bits, Physical = 17 bits",
                "Logical = 17 bits, Physical = 18 bits",
                "Logical = 11 bits, Physical = 11 bits",
                "Logical = 7 bits, Physical = 6 bits"
              ],
              "a": 0,
              "why": "128 pages = 2^7 (7 bits), 2048 words = 2^11 (11 offset bits), 64 frames = 2^6 (6 bits). Logical = 7 + 11 = 18 bits; Physical = 6 + 11 = 17 bits."
            },
            {
              "type": "mcq",
              "q": "2 (Q53). Consider a machine with 64 MB physical memory and a 32-bit virtual address space. If the page size is 4 KB, what is the approximate number of entries in the page table (and size if each entry is 2 bytes)?",
              "o": [
                "2^20 entries (1M entries); 2 MB page table",
                "2^16 entries; 16 MB page table",
                "2^12 entries; 4 KB page table",
                "2^24 entries; 24 MB page table"
              ],
              "a": 0,
              "why": "Page size = 4 KB = 2^12 bytes. Number of pages in 32-bit virtual space = 2^32 / 2^12 = 2^20 entries (1M entries). At 2 bytes per entry, size = 2 MB (or 4 MB at 4 bytes/entry)."
            },
            {
              "type": "mcq",
              "q": "3 (Q56). In a paged memory, the page hit ratio in the TLB is 0.85 (85%). The time required to access a page in main memory is 90 ms, and TLB lookup time is negligible (0). What is the Effective Access Time (EAT)?",
              "o": [
                "90.0 ms",
                "103.5 ms",
                "135.0 ms",
                "180.0 ms"
              ],
              "a": 1,
              "why": "EAT = 0.85 × 90 + (1 - 0.85) × (2 × 90) = 76.5 + 0.15 × 180 = 76.5 + 27.0 = 103.5 ms."
            },
            {
              "type": "mcq",
              "q": "4 (Q67–70). For the 19-page reference string `7, 0, 1, 2, 0, 3, 0, 4, 2, 3, 0, 3, 2, 1, 2, 0, 1, 7, 0` with 3 initially empty frames, what are the page fault counts under FIFO, Optimal, and LRU (and hit count under Optimal)?",
              "o": [
                "FIFO = 14 faults, Optimal = 9 faults (10 hits), LRU = 12 faults",
                "FIFO = 15 faults, Optimal = 12 faults, LRU = 9 faults",
                "FIFO = 9 faults, Optimal = 14 faults, LRU = 12 faults",
                "FIFO = 12 faults, Optimal = 10 faults, LRU = 14 faults"
              ],
              "a": 0,
              "why": "On the 19-reference string (missing the final '1' from Slide 9.21), FIFO has 14 faults (5 hits), Optimal has 9 faults (10 hits), and LRU has 12 faults (7 hits)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
